      <h1>What data do AI teams buy?</h1>
      <p class="lead">Not raw files. AI teams look for records that show how real work was done, decided and corrected over time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 class="reveal">What makes records useful</h2>
      <ol class="path reveal">
        <li>
          <h3>A decision, not just an outcome</h3>
          <p>The question, the options considered and the reason for the choice are what make a record teachable.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>History, not a snapshot</h3>
          <p>Earlier versions and corrections show how thinking changed, which a single export cannot.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Variety across systems</h3>
          <p>Chat, tickets, documents and CRM notes each reveal a different part of the same piece of work.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

