  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 class="reveal">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq reveal">
        <details><summary>Do AI teams want my whole archive?</summary><p>Rarely. Scope is usually a defined slice: certain systems, certain years, certain kinds of record, with personal information handled separately.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is one system enough?</summary><p>Not usually. The data buyer looks for at least five systems holding the work, because context across tools is what makes records usable.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does more data always mean more value?</summary><p>No. Coherent records with context are worth more than a large, messy export. We do not publish prices, because it depends on the data and the terms.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

